{
    "en": {
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_NAME": "Interrogator",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_SUBTITLE": "Torment Specialist",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_PASSIVE_NAME": "Torment",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_PASSIVE_DESCRIPTION": "Interrogator can hit and be hit by allies and enemies. Attackers who hit Interrogator are marked Guilty.",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_PRIMARY_SWING_DESCRIPTION": "Swing your baton in front, causing <style=cIsDamage>320% damage</style>. Missing the attack causes you to suffer <style=cIsDamage>damage</style> instead.",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_SECONDARY_AFFRAY_DESCRIPTION": "Throw a cleaver that deals <style=cIsDamage>450% damage</style>. <style=cIsDamage>Slayer.</style> If the cleaver kills the target, applies Hemorrhage and Pressure on all in the area.",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_UTILITY_FALSIFY_DESCRIPTION": "Dash forward dealing <style=cIsDamage>390% damage</style> and applying Guilty on hit targets.",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_SPECIAL_CONVICT_NAME": "Convict",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_SPECIAL_CONVICT_DESCRIPTION": "Duel a Guilty enemy for 10 seconds. Your primary no longer hits you and grants a stack of Guilty on hit. During the duel, external damage to you is negated, but damage to other enemies besides the target is also negated.",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_SPECIAL_SCEPTER_CONVICT_NAME": "Punish",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_SPECIAL_SCEPTER_CONVICT_DESCRIPTION": "Duel a Guilty enemy for 10 seconds. Your primary no longer hits you and grants a stack of Guilty on hit. During the duel, external damage to you is negated, but damage to other enemies besides the target is also negated.\n<color=#d299ff>SCEPTER: Convict can target enemies without Guilty. Damage you deal is no longer negated, but is reduced by 75%.</color>",
        "MASTERY_SKIN_NAME": "Interrogator: Specialist",
        "<style=cKeywordName>Slayer</style><style=cSub>Deals up to <style=cIsDamage>3x</style> damage against low health enemies.</style>": "<style=cKeywordName>Slayer</style><style=cSub>Deals up to <style=cIsDamage>3x</style> damage against low-health enemies.</style>",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_DESCRIPTION": "The Interrogator revels in the pain of others. Don't have too much fun hurting your allies... or do.<color=#CCD3E0>\n\n< ! > Get hit by enemies, allies, and even yourself to gain bonus stats. No one is safe.\n\n< ! > If you have items that trigger when you are hit, use Affray to inflict Hemorrhage on yourself. No pain, no gain.\n\n< ! > Falsify is a great way to force enemies to be marked Guilty. Unethical? What do you mean?\n\n< ! > Convict a Guilty target to make sure they are punished. Guilty until proven innocent, after all.</color>",
        "<style=cKeywordName>Guilty</style><style=cSub>Grants <color=#FFBF66>Interrogator</color> <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style>, <style=cIsHealing>health regen</style>, and <style=cIsDamage>damage</style> for each <color=#FFBF66>Guilty</color> target.</style>": "<style=cKeywordName>Guilty</style><style=cSub>Each Guilty target grants Interrogator attack speed, health regeneration and damage.</style>",
        "<style=cKeywordName>Ally Damage</style><style=cSub>Allies take and deal less damage to each other and <color=#FFBF66>Guilty</color> expires from them after 10 seconds.</style>": "<style=cKeywordName>Ally Damage</style><style=cSub>Allies deal and receive less damage from each other; Guilty expires from them after 10 seconds.</style>",
        "<style=cKeywordName>Hemorrhage</style><style=cSub>Deal <style=cIsDamage>2000%</style> base damage over 15s. <i>Hemorrhage</i> can stack.</style>": "<style=cKeywordName>Hemorrhage</style><style=cSub>Deals 2000% base damage over 15 seconds. Hemorrhage can stack.</style>",
        "<style=cKeywordName>Pressured</style><style=cSub>Boost <style=cIsDamage>attack speed</style> and <style=cIsUtility>move speed</style> but lowers <style=cIsHealing>armor</style> and <style=cIsDamage>damage</style>.</style>": "<style=cKeywordName>Pressured</style><style=cSub>Increases attack and movement speed, but reduces armor and damage.</style>",
        "KENKO_INTERROGATOR_LORE": "Snow softly fell from the skies, as was usual for the region that Dylan had found himself in. He, with his squad, stood on duty, looking out for either danger, or someone who needed rescue.\n\n\"Sir, I think I see someone.\" The private turned around to face his superior. The commander didn’t turn around at first, only grunting. His voice was tired. The sheer amount of people lost to this planet had begun to exhaust even people like him, a veteran of the 2019 War. This rescue operation had been a disaster so far, and that’s excluding what happened to the crew of the Contact Light.\n\n\"It’s a person, I’m certain,\" The soldier continued, turning back to face the vast white hollow, with the occasional tree scattered around. And he was correct: it was a person, lazily strolling through snow. The weather last night was nightmarish: the elemental assault of the planet had covered the valley in a higher-than-knee deep layer of cold carpet, and only the top part of the figure was visible. \n\nDylan raised his head from the binoculars to see that his commander was finally facing in the same direction as him.\n\n\"Sir, should we send someone?\" Dylan inquired.\n\n\"No,\" replied his commander.\n\nThe private turned back to the landscape for a moment. \"Why?\"\n\n\"It's not a human.\"\n\n\"..Sure looks like one,\" the private said as he peered back through the binoculars.\n\n\"Not a living one, at the very least.\"\n\n\"... You think that planet could raise the dead?\"\n\n\"I wouldn't be surprised\"\n\nThe soldier kept looking through his binoculars. The longer he looked at the stranger, the more apparent the oddities that threw off his higher up became. The lone wanderer was wearing a big, black jacket, the hood of which had thick dirty fur. The man was well-prepared for cold weather, save for the fact that the sleeves of the jacket were torn off, exposing his arms. He turned slightly, allowing the private a look at his torso: they were wearing a standard-issued chest plate, just like the one the private had on his chest, but it was an older model, probably outdated by a year or more. The orange paint was completely chipped away, leaving the heavily scratched black metallic surface exposed. The helmet looked like it matched the chestplate; standard issue commando gear, a bit out of date. The color had been slightly bleached by the sun.\n\nWhoever- or whatever it was, it seemed like a ruse. A mimic, luring people in. As if something was trying to play human, but didn’t understand what made something human in the first place.\n\n\"…Yeah, sir. You’re probably right.\"\n\nWhat they found the next morning made that thing seem even less human. A squad of soldiers that Dylan was part of was sent on a scouting mission, and remembering what transpired yesterday, the private convinced his comrades and commander to investigate as to where, or from where, the figure was walking. The trail of footsteps led them to a brutal scene: a torn down Contact Light camp. It was a small one that had no more than 5 people. 5 poor souls murdered in ways that eyes could never truly comprehend, in a way that no human being should be able to. And yet, there were no bite marks, no claw marks, no scales, pieces of tar or fur, no blood samples of native species: nothing was alien. Everything was human."
    }
}
